592186045417] [17592186050865 #edb/ref 1027 #edb/ref 17592186049806 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050865 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186064150 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050865 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186064151 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050865 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186064275 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050865 #edb/ref 1031 "Removing Point Discontinuities" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050865 #edb/ref 1033 341 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050865 #edb/ref 1035 #uuid "6c838d5e-1457-5ed8-957b-544017d2ddfe" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186076496 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186076497 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186076496 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186076498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186076496 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186076499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186076496 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186076500 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186076496 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186076501 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186076496 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186076496 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186076496 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "351ba727-ee60-5614-b40f-f04d04640276" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186076497 #edb/ref 1080 "DNE" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186076497 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186076497 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "8836b938-9934-5409-9f10-b4cd7ecd94f5" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186076498 #edb/ref 1080 "\\frac{1}{4}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186076498 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186076498 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "8b54c412-bad4-597e-8f0a-6225d88f3773" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186076499 #edb/ref 1080 "4" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186076499 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186076499 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "9e409971-c2d3-5b6e-82ee-3468d654e307" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186076500 #edb/ref 1080 "\\frac{1}{2}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186076500 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186076500 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "d8a5d0a3-5345-59e8-a53d-391d532ea4ee" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186076501 #edb/ref 1080 "0" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186076501 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186076501 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "53a20335-f8bf-5362-b368-968fcc33eef5" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186078358 #edb/ref 1069 "e-74" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186078358 #edb/ref 1071 "Evaluate $\\displaystyle{\\lim_{x \\to 4^+} \\dfrac {x - 2\\sqrt{x}} {x - 4} }.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186078358 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "06d5e05a-4595-551f-8c1b-7c585f69b47b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186078358 #edb/ref 1074 "If we attempt to evaluate the limit, we get an indeterminate form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to {4}^{+}}\\frac{x-2\\sqrt{x}}{x-4} & =\\frac{4-2\\sqrt{4}}{4-4}=\\frac{0}{0},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we need to first simplify the limit. Since the radical is in the numerator, we can multiply the numerator and the denominator by the conjugate of the numerator. We get\n\n$$\n\\eqalign{\n\t\\lim_{x \\to 4^+} \\dfrac {x - 2\\sqrt{x}} {x - 4} &= \\lim_{x \\to 4^+} \\dfrac {(x -2 \\sqrt{x})(x+2\\sqrt x)} {(x - 4)(x+2\\sqrt x)} \\\n            &= \\lim_{x \\to 4^+} \\dfrac {x^2-\\left(2\\sqrt{x}\\right)^2} {(x - 4)(x+2\\sqrt x)} \\\n\t    &= \\lim_{x \\to 4^+} \\dfrac {x^2-4x} {(x - 4)(x+2\\sqrt x)} \\\n\t    &= \\lim_{x \\to 4^+} \\dfrac {x(x-4)} {(x - 4)(x+2\\sqrt x)} \\\n\t    &= \\lim_{x \\to 4^+} \\dfrac {x} {x+2\\sqrt x} \\\n\t    &= \\lim_{x \\to 4^+} \\dfrac {4} {4+2\\sqrt4} \\\n\t    &=\\dfrac 1 2.\n\t}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186078359 #edb/ref 1069 "e-75" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186078359 #edb/ref 1071 "Calculate $\\displaystyle{\\lim_{x \\to 0} \\dfrac {3x} {\\sqrt{x +1} -1}  }.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186078359 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "7db311cd-70a0-50f4-8984-4a578abc67eb" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186078359 #edb/ref 1074 "If we attempt to evaluate the limit by simply evaluating the function at $x=0$, we get an indeterminate form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to 0}\\frac{3x}{\\sqrt{x+1}-1} & =\\frac{3\\cdot 0}{\\sqrt{0+1}-1}=\\frac{0}{0}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we need to first simplify the limit. Since the radical is in the denominator, we can multiply the numerator and the denominator by the conjugate of the denominator. We get\n\n$$\n\\eqalign{\n\\lim_{x \\to 0} \\dfrac {3x} {\\sqrt{x + 1} - 1} \n\t&=\\lim_{x\\to 0}\\frac{(3x)(\\sqrt{x+1}+1)}{(\\sqrt{x + 1} - 1)(\\sqrt{x+1}+1)}\\\n\t&=\\lim_{x\\to 0}\\frac{3x(\\sqrt{x+1}+1)}{\\left(\\sqrt{x+1}\\right)^2-1^2}\\\n\t&=\\lim_{x\\to 0}\\frac{3x(\\sqrt{x+1}+1)}{x+1-1}\\\n\t&=\\lim_{x\\to 0}\\frac{3x(\\sqrt{x+1}+1)}{x}\\\n\t&=\\lim_{x\\to 0}3(\\sqrt{x+1}+1)\\\n&=3(\\sqrt{0+1}+1)\\\n\t&=6.\n}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186078536 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186048758 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186078536 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186049927 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186078536 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186078923 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186078536 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186078926 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186078536 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186233047 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186078536 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186233048 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186078536 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186233093 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186078536 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186233546 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186078536 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186233883 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186078536 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186233884 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186078536 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186233885 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186078536 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186234058 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186078536 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186235413 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186078536 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186244012 #edb/ref